// check: accepted
// CROWN modal (§11 6.3's crucible sweep): the ABSOLUTE MODALITY — a
// Pure value transports across worlds unchanged. The closure g performs
// nothing; it is born inside an extent that ALSO performs E (absorbed
// by h at the install), escapes, and is called under a declared !E.
// Its row is its BODY's row, never its birthplace's ambient — the
// []-boxed dual of leak-escape-negation, which refuses the E-performing
// twin of this same shape. Expect NO E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(1) }
fn birth() = {
  let g = () => 2
  let primed = op()
  g
} ~> h
fn use() with !E = birth()()
fn main() = use()
